children.push(p("Rehearse short, confident answers to the questions a panel is most likely to ask. Below are the common ones with the line of reasoning to take."));
children.push(bullet("**Why not just use keyword matching?** It misses semantically related skills — a TensorFlow project not matched to a machine-learning role. Sentence-BERT captures meaning, which my results quantify against a TF-IDF baseline."));
children.push(bullet("**Why Random Forest and not deep learning for ranking?** With a limited local dataset, tree ensembles are more robust, less prone to overfitting, train fast, and give feature importance for explainability — all of which suit a final-year scope."));
children.push(bullet("**How do you handle bias and fairness?** Skills-based features only, no protected attributes in the model, fairness checks across groups, and transparent, logged scoring so recommendations can be audited."));
children.push(bullet("**Why is this better than LinkedIn or Indeed?** Local terminology in the skill dictionary, semantic matching tuned to Nepali IT resumes, and a free, lightweight stack — the local fit global platforms do not provide."));
